= Regulation

== The 2020 Amendments

#slide[
  === The SEC treated proxy advice as a solicitation, and then backed away.
  #inv("A5")

  - The 2020 amendments conditioned the exemptions on notice to the issuer.

  #quote(block: true)[The term solicitation includes ... the furnishing of a form of proxy or other communication to security holders under circumstances reasonably calculated to result in the procurement, withholding or revocation of a proxy.]

  #callout[The paper's sample ends in 2019, before either rule took effect; nothing on this slide is an estimate of their effect.]

  - The 2022 rescission removed the notice conditions but kept the definition.
]
